

Add unit tests – test the product service and its business logic without requiring a database.
Implement Spring Security with JWT – authentication, registration, and stateless authorization.
Implement role-based access control (RBAC) – customers and administrators have different permissions.
Build the order and checkout modules.
Add integration tests before moving to the frontend.

#########################################COMMANDS###############################################################
- start node js container in project directory: npm.cmd run dev
- run redis on docker: docker run -d --name ecommerce-redis  -p 6379:6379 redis:7
- check running containers: docker ps
- test the container : docker exec -it <container name> redis-cli ping

- connect to redis in docker container to run commands on it : docker exec -it <container name> redis-cli
- list all the keys in the cache on redis: KEYS *
- get the value of a key: GET "<KEY>"
- get remaining time of the value : TTL "<KEY>"
- DEL <cacheName>::<id>